> is upside down and "mirrored" (as if viewed in a mirror).  Its easily
> seen when looking at the GeneChip name in the image.

The function "image" plots the thing using the "X" and "Y" coordinates
given in CEL files. It happens that the result is the reflection
of what one would see when looking at the chip. An effort was made
to correct that at an earliest stage of the development of the package,
but I droped that as we played more with indexing of elements in Cel
object (in order to save some sanity). It did not appear to be 
very important (for visual things with the image, you may want
to look at the function plotLocation)... but if it does just let
me know.


